## 3. Schemes compared (`results/helios_n_partition_m68.csv`)

| Scheme | n | max \|S\| | cross edges | Verdict |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| **by_time_only** | 4 | **28** | 16 | **Reject** for Yosys — mid times 28>16 |
| **intra_time_det_pack** | **6** | **14** | 24 | **Chosen** — all parts ≤16 |
| node_id_shards | 5 | 16 | 58 | Reject — ignores DEM / Helios topology |

**Chosen algorithm:** along Stim detector **time** (Helios-like round axis); within each time, greedily pack detectors so \|dets ∪ their boundaries\| ≤ N_phys=16.

**Parts (summary):** see `results/helios_n_partition_m68_parts.csv` — sizes 8,14,14,14,14,8.

**Cross-cuts:** 24 unique undirected edges in `results/helios_n_partition_m68_crosscuts.csv`. Helios rule: for each cross edge \((u,v)\), map virtual PEs \(u\) and \(v\) to the **same** physical PE so neighbor state stays in that PE’s LUTRAM (no Heer extra lattice wires).

**n lower bound:** \(\lceil V/16\rceil=5\); chosen **n=6** (topology pack > pure capacity bound).

